WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.034
-My next guest is an Emmy-

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.903
and Grammy-nominated
actor and comedian.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.672
You can see him in the show
"Schmigadoon!"

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.774
New episodes are available
Fridays on Apple TV+.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:11.177
Here is Fred Armisen.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.546
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:19.185
♪♪

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.254
-I don't --
-[ Laughing ]

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.622
-I don't have --
I didn't have glue.

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:26.192
-Oh, my --
-Dammit.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.728
-Can you lean back, maybe?
How's it going, man?

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:30.997
-It's pretty good.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.365
I'm at the dentist.

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.667
-You're at the dentist
right now?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.602
-Yeah, it's my dentist's office,
man.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:40.306
-Why couldn't you
Zoom me from home?

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.442
-This is the appointments.
They were just at the same time.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:44.243
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:45.845
-I love that
you have mustaches around.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.046
Fred, how are you doing?
I miss you.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.948
Nice to see you.
-I miss you.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.517
How you been?
Hi.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.318
-I'm fantastic.
Hi, bud.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.354
Yeah, I got this silly
mustache and beard.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.656
This is a fake, Fred.

00:00:57.656 --> 00:00:59.025
-It is?
-Yeah.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.993
[ Laughter ]
I was kidding.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.196
I was doing a joke.
Fred, have you been back

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.432
to 30 Rock since the --
since the pandemic?

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:07.934
-No, I have not been back.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.703
It's been,
you know, over like a year.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.971
Year and three months
or something.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.741
-We miss you, bud.
Do you remember your first day

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:18.544
in 30 Rock, or first time
you came into the building?

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.180
-First time I ever went
to 30 Rock was to see

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.019
a dress rehearsal
of "SNL" in 1982.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.587
Because a classmate of mine,

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.256
her dad was
a cameraman on "SNL,"

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.924
and The Clash
were gonna be on.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.560
So, she was like, "Yeah,
I know you like The Clash.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.462
Why don't you go see them?"
And I did.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.498
It was incredible.
-No way.

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:40.966
You ended up doing --
I remember you did a sketch

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:43.236
with them for something,

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.471
where you were
eating rubbish or whatever.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.206
You were a character --
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:48.541
Yeah.
-What was that for?

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.376
That was --
-That was for Funny or Die,

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.979
and they were promoting, like,
this box set of theirs.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.048
And I told them
that I went to go see them.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.116
I was like -- you know, I was,
like, being really earnest.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:58.684
Like, "Yeah, you know,
I actually went

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.986
to go see you guys at 'SNL,'"

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:03.189
and they kind of made fun of me
a little bit.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.190
They did a bit
where they were like,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.192
"Oh, yeah, I remember you."

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.394
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.762
-That's what you want from them.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.030
-That's what you want, though.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.199
-Yeah, that's what you want.
They're rock stars.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.435
-"Oh, right, yeah,
you were in the crowd."

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:18.370
-"Yeah, you were the one
clappin', right?

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.839
In the audience?
I remember you."

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.574
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.576
That's a good bit.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.411
Dude, I know
you just came from Italy.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.047
You're shooting with our pal,
Molly Shannon.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.649
How's Molly Shannon?
-Yeah.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.017
Oh, she's great.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:34.420
I feel like Molly Shannon
is someone who everybody loves.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.089
You know?
Like, I always think like, "Oh,"

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.524
like, you know,
"That's like my friend."

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.059
And then it turns out
everyone loves her.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.527
So she's very hypnotizing.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.597
Like, when you talk to her,
she draws you in.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.365
[ Light laughter ]
"Yeah!"

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:49.335
-[ Laughing ]
She does do that.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.303
You're like,
"I was thinking that, too."

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:52.572
Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.106
-She's the greatest.
Well, I know that you're --

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:57.076
you're back doing stand-up,
which is exciting.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.711
-Yes.
-This is a big deal.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.780
[ Cheers and applause ]
So go see Fred.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.248
Can you set up --

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.484
What can we expect in
a Fred Armisen stand-up special?

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.153
-Well, I've been
doing this thing

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:10.657
where I do strumming styles
from around the world.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.524
-Strumming styles
from around the world.

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:14.360
-This is, like, basically,
kind of folk kind of rock,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.494
but this is, like --

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:18.197
this is how they
strum a guitar in Australia.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.765
So they're very confident.
They're like...

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:22.368
[ Guitar strumming ]

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.436
♪ You better believe it ♪

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:25.804
♪ Believe what you say ♪

00:03:25.804 --> 00:03:27.339
You know, they're
very sort of like...

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:29.008
fast chord changes.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:32.211
And then, Canada's a little --
Canada's like a little wispier

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:35.047
and, like, a little more
sort of elaborate, like...

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:39.485
[ Guitar strumming ]

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.221
♪ Don't you know
it's my window again ♪

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:43.389
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.758
That kind of thing.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.827
The U.S.A. is --
You know, the strumming style

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:50.496
is very...
[ Guitar strumming ]

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:55.234
♪♪

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.904
And Americans like to pretend
like they can't hit a note

00:03:58.904 --> 00:04:00.039
when they sing.
It's a...

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:03.075
[ Creaky voice ]
♪ Don't you know ♪

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.511
♪ It's a jar ♪

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.246
♪ Again ♪

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.082
♪ I know ♪

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.983
♪ Again ♪

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.485
♪ Tomorrow ♪

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.754
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:15.888
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.489
-♪ Again ♪

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:21.494
♪ You know ♪
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.996
-Brazil.
Brazil is very close.

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:25.464
It sounds like the microphone's
right on them.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:26.531
So it's like...

00:04:26.531 --> 00:04:28.101
[ Singing in Portuguese ]

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.403
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.304
-Oh, my God.

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:33.405
♪♪

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:35.975
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.843
You are so funny.
-Colombia is very percussive.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:40.679
♪♪

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:43.082
[ Singing in Spanish ]

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.717
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.520
And then, Italy,
they like to do sort of

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.723
mid-tempo, a little slower
and they're like sort of...

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:51.757
[ Guitar strumming ]

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.160
[ Singing in Italian ]

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.028
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.028 --> 00:05:00.833
♪♪

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.368
Ireland is very --

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.503
Ireland only likes to do
one chord. Just...

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:08.174
[ Guitar strumming ]

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.741
[ Rapping desk ]

00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:11.977
[ Singing Gibberish ]

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:18.184
♪♪

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.585
-Yeah.
One, two, three, four!

00:05:20.585 --> 00:05:24.857
[ Singing gibberish ]

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:26.559
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:30.162
♪♪

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:31.797
One, two, three, four!

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:33.632
♪♪

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:35.534
-That's it.
That's some of it.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.336
-That's is in a nutshell
what we have to --

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:39.504
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.504 --> 00:05:42.074
You are unbelievable.

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:44.042
Fred, can we talk about
"Schmigadoon"?

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:46.713
This is on Apple TV+.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.648
I love the premise.
Basically, it's

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:51.216
Keegan-Michael Key,
Cecily Strong are a couple.

00:05:51.216 --> 00:05:53.786
They get -- They go for a hike.
They're in a fight.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.822
And they end up getting stuck
into a magical world

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:59.558
that is set in --
it's all musicals.

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:04.029
And they have to find true love
to escape this musical world.

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:05.631
-Yeah.
-I think you're perfect

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:08.300
to be in it.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.035
Here's Fred Armisen
in "Schmigadoon."

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:11.603
Take a look at this.

00:06:11.603 --> 00:06:13.005
-Unfortunately,
no one seems to be interested

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.874
in my rhubarb squares.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.242
-Oh, I love rhubarb squares.

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:19.311
-You do?
Me, too!

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:21.814
-And I thought
I was the only one.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:24.783
-Well, they're definitely
not for everybody.

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:27.253
[ Coin rattles ]
-I'll take two.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:31.090
-Wonderful.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:34.026
-Here.
I'd hate to enjoy it alone.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.595
-Oh, thank you.

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:39.098
-Eh, eh, eh, Howard.
Don't forget your diet.

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:40.499
We don't want to have
to get your fat pants

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:41.968
out from the attic again.

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:45.604
-Oh.
Sorry, Mildred.

00:06:45.604 --> 00:06:47.473
-That's what I'm talking about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.308
-Fat pants.
-That is Fred Armisen,

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:51.444
the one and only!
Oh, we love you, Fred.

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:52.944
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I love you. Thank you.

00:06:52.944 --> 00:06:55.080
-New episodes of "Schmigadoon"
are available Fridays

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.083
on Apple TV+.

